{
  "name": "Lead Capture → Qualification → CRM",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🟢 TRIGGER\n**Webhook Node**\n\nEntry point for the whole workflow. Connect this URL to:\n- Website contact/inquiry form\n- Facebook Lead Ads\n- WhatsApp Business API\n\nFires instantly when a new lead submits their details.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_1",
      "name": "Note: 1. Webhook - Lead In",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1420,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📋 STEP 1\n**Capture Raw Lead Data**\n\nNormalizes the incoming payload into clean fields:\n`name, phone, email, budget, location, propertyType, source, timestamp`\n\nEverything downstream reads from these fields — keep names consistent with your form.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_2",
      "name": "Note: 2. Capture Raw Lead Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1180,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🤖 STEP 2\n**AI Qualification (Claude)**\n\nSends the lead's message + budget to Claude.\n\nPrompt asks it to:\n- Classify as **Hot / Warm / Cold**\n- Summarize intent in 1 line\n\nReturns raw JSON in the response body — parsed in the next node.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "sticky_3",
      "name": "Note: 3. AI Qualification (Claude)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -940,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔧 Helper\n**Parse AI Output**\n\nExtracts `score` and `summary` from Claude's JSON reply and merges them back onto the original lead record.\n\nFalls back to \"Warm\" + a manual-review note if the AI response isn't valid JSON, so nothing gets silently dropped.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "sticky_4",
      "name": "Note: 4. Parse AI Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔀 STEP 3\n**Conditional Routing (Switch)**\n\nRoutes the lead down 1 of 3 paths based on `score`:\n- **Hot** → instant alert + call link\n- **Warm** → nurture sequence (Workflow 2)\n- **Cold** → newsletter list only\n\nAll 3 branches reconverge before the CRM push.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "sticky_5",
      "name": "Note: 5. Route by Lead Score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔥 HOT branch\n**Generate Call Link**\n\nBuilds a pre-filled Cal.com/Calendly booking URL using the lead's name + email, so the agent can send it straight in the Slack alert.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "sticky_6",
      "name": "Note: 6a. Generate Call Link",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔥 STEP 3a (Hot)\n**Slack Instant Alert**\n\nPosts to `#hot-leads` immediately: name, phone, budget, location, AI summary, and the booking link.\n\nGoal: agent sees and can act on a hot lead within minutes.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "sticky_7",
      "name": "Note: 6b. Slack Instant Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        20,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🌤 STEP 3b (Warm)\n**Send to Nurture Sequence**\n\nForwards the lead to Workflow 2 via webhook — a drip sequence (email/WhatsApp over days/weeks) instead of an instant push.\n\nSwap the URL once Workflow 2 exists.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "sticky_8",
      "name": "Note: 6c. Send to Workflow 2 (Nurture)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ❄️ STEP 3c (Cold)\n**Add to Newsletter List**\n\nLow-intent leads skip active outreach and just get appended to a monthly newsletter sheet — no agent time spent chasing them.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 220,
        "color": 8
      },
      "id": "sticky_9",
      "name": "Note: 6d. Add to Newsletter List",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        500
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🗂 STEP 4\n**CRM Push**\n\nEvery lead — regardless of score — gets logged here with score, source, and timestamp.\n\nThis is your single source of truth. Swap for Airtable/HubSpot if preferred.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_10",
      "name": "Note: 7. CRM Push (Google Sheets)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 💬 STEP 5\n**Instant Auto-Reply**\n\nSends the lead a personalized WhatsApp message acknowledging their inquiry and referencing their location + budget, so they hear back within seconds even before an agent responds.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_11",
      "name": "Note: 8. Instant Auto-Reply (WhatsApp)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔔 STEP 6\n**Internal Notification**\n\nPosts a summary of every logged lead to `#lead-notifications` so the agent has a running feed and never misses one — this is the general log, separate from the urgent Hot alert in Step 3a.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_12",
      "name": "Note: 9. Internal Notification",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        680,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lead-capture",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "webhook_1",
      "name": "1. Webhook - Lead In",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -1400,
        300
      ],
      "webhookId": "lead-capture"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "name",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.name }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "phone",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.phone }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "email",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.email }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "budget",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.budget }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a5",
              "name": "location",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.location }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a6",
              "name": "propertyType",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.propertyType }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a7",
              "name": "source",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.source || 'website' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a8",
              "name": "timestamp",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "set_1",
      "name": "2. Capture Raw Lead Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "anthropic-version",
              "value": "2023-06-01"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\n  model: \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n  max_tokens: 300,\n  messages: [{\n    role: \"user\",\n    content: `You are a real estate lead qualification assistant. Based on this lead's details, classify them as Hot, Warm, or Cold and summarize their intent in 1 line. Respond ONLY with valid JSON in this exact format: {\"score\": \"Hot|Warm|Cold\", \"summary\": \"one line summary\"}.\\n\\nLead details:\\nName: ${$json.name}\\nBudget: ${$json.budget}\\nLocation preference: ${$json.location}\\nProperty type: ${$json.propertyType}`\n  }]\n}) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "http_ai_1",
      "name": "3. AI Qualification (Claude)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        -920,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Anthropic API Key Header"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const raw = $input.first().json.content[0].text;\nlet parsed;\ntry {\n  parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n} catch (e) {\n  parsed = { score: 'Warm', summary: 'Could not parse AI response - manual review needed' };\n}\n\nconst lead = $('2. Capture Raw Lead Data').first().json;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...lead,\n    score: parsed.score,\n    summary: parsed.summary\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "code_1",
      "name": "4. Parse AI Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -680,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict"
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c1",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.score }}",
                    "rightValue": "Hot",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Hot"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict"
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c2",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.score }}",
                    "rightValue": "Warm",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Warm"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict"
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c3",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.score }}",
                    "rightValue": "Cold",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Cold"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "fallbackOutput": "extra"
        }
      },
      "id": "switch_1",
      "name": "5. Route by Lead Score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "typeVersion": 3.2,
      "position": [
        -440,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "b1",
              "name": "callLink",
              "value": "=https://cal.com/your-agency/consult?name={{ encodeURIComponent($json.name) }}&email={{ encodeURIComponent($json.email) }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "set_calllink",
      "name": "6a. Generate Call Link",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        -200,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "hot-leads"
        },
        "text": "=🔥 *HOT LEAD*: {{ $json.name }} | {{ $json.phone }} | Budget: {{ $json.budget }} | {{ $json.location }}\nSummary: {{ $json.summary }}\nBook a call: {{ $json.callLink }}",
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "id": "slack_hot",
      "name": "6b. Slack Instant Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
